WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.590
An amoeba is a single cell.

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.520
No lungs.

3
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.420
No heart.

4
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.660
No blood.

5
00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.810
Oxygen simply diffuses
in across its surface,

6
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.640
and carbon dioxide diffuses out.

7
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:16.720
Every living cell needs that same
swap, in an amoeba or in you.

8
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.910
So why can an amoeba survive
without lungs or a heart,

9
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.440
when you can't?

10
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.100
In this mission, you'll grow
a cube to 10 times its width,

11
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.960
keep its shape, and watch
its surface and its volume.

12
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.990
Then you'll take one fixed volume,
squash it into a flat sheet,

13
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.720
and see what changes.

14
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.270
Your mission: explain why an amoeba
can survive without lungs or a heart,

15
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.360
but you can't.
